{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "Service Level Objectives, control-plane, queue, runner and telemetry health from agentsfleetd. Panels 20-25 are the SLO view; everything below panel 4 is the operator view.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "Share of admission attempts that were accepted rather than deferred or refused, over the dashboard range. Target 99%, unproven \u2014 it was set against 14 events. Below target means callers are being turned away: check the backpressure and backlog panels next.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.99
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 20,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome=~\"appended|replayed\"}[$__range])) / sum(increase(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome!=\"over_budget\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "availability",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Are we accepting work?",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "Runs that finished cleanly, over runs the PLATFORM was accountable for. A failure caused by the workload \u2014 policy_deny, landlock_deny, oom_kill, resource_kill, budget_breach, timeout_kill \u2014 is excluded from the denominator entirely: it is neither a success nor a breach, because the platform delivered and what it ran did not. That keeps one tenant's bad code from spending everybody's error budget, and stops a noisy tenant diluting the ratio and hiding real platform failures behind volume. An unclassified failure counts as ours. Target 95%, UNPROVEN \u2014 set against 10 executions, of which all 3 failures were platform-caused, so this split does not move today's number. 'How runs are ending' below breaks the failures out by reason.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.95
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 21,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(agentsfleet_runner_executions_total{outcome=\"processed\"}[$__range])) / sum(increase(agentsfleet_runner_executions_total{fault!=\"workload\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "success",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Are runs finishing cleanly? (platform faults only)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "Fraction of sampled minutes in which the oldest unconfirmed admission was younger than the replay floor (60s, derived from MIN_AGE + INTERVAL in afd_runner/src/sweep/replay.rs). This measures OBSERVED TIME, not work items: it does not say what share of admissions were picked up inside 60s. It reads N/A when the gauge is absent rather than inventing a pass, so a blank here means no telemetry, not compliance.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.99
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 22,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "avg_over_time((max(agentsfleet_admission_backlog_oldest_age_seconds) < bool __ADMISSION_REPLAY_FLOOR_SECONDS__)[$__range:1m])",
          "legendFormat": "within floor",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Time the backlog stayed under the replay floor",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "Age of the freshest heartbeat from the runner that is furthest behind. Per-runner tables are in-process and never evicted, so this takes min-by-runner first, then the worst of those \u2014 either half alone pages for a healthy fleet. Above the offline threshold, that runner is gone.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": "__RUNNER_OFFLINE_SECONDS_NUM__"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 23,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max(min by (runner_id) (time() - agentsfleet_runner_last_seen_seconds))",
          "legendFormat": "worst age",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Has any runner gone quiet?",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "description": "Fresh run-starts divided by appended admissions over the range. APPROXIMATE, AND NOT COHORT-CORRECT: a start inside the range need not belong to an admission inside the range, so boundary lag can push this above 100%, invent a failure at the end of a range, or show success from admissions made hours earlier. No PromQL fixes that \u2014 it needs an admission terminal-outcome counter, or an admit-to-start histogram, or a gauge of admitted-but-unstarted fleets with an oldest age. Until one exists this is a smell test, never an objective, and nothing alerts on it. It also reads empty until a daemon carrying both families is deployed.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 4,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.99
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 34,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(agentsfleet_fleet_runs_started_total{kind=\"fresh\"}[$__range])) / sum(increase(agentsfleet_admissions_total{outcome=\"appended\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "started / admitted",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Approximate starts over admissions (not an objective)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "id": 37,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "All-cause run success (not an objective)",
      "description": "The same ratio WITHOUT the blame split: every failure counted, including the ones the workload caused. This is what a customer feels \u2014 'did my run work' is a fair question with a real answer. It carries no target and nothing alerts on it, because an objective has to be a promise about something this platform controls. Read it beside the objective to its left: a wide gap between them is tenants shipping code that fails, not a platform regression.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "__PROMETHEUS_UID__"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "all-cause success",
          "expr": "sum(increase(agentsfleet_runner_executions_total{outcome=\"processed\"}[$__range])) / sum(increase(agentsfleet_runner_executions_total[$__range]))"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 3,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
